// ---- Main Loop ----

/// Main loop of the interface. Call this repeatedly from one thread for as long as the stack is
/// running;
/// nothing is sent or received between calls.
///
/// CALL CADENCE. There is no fixed requirement, but Tick() is the only pump for inbound frames,
/// the
/// data-link and BBMD loops, confirmed-request retries and timeouts, COV, trend logging and alarm
/// evaluation. Ticking slowly delays every one of those: peers see late responses, timeouts fire
/// late,
/// and inbound frames are dropped once the host's socket buffer fills. Aim for every 10-100 ms
/// for a
/// typical device; go faster if you need tight COV or alarm latency.
///
/// REQUIRED CALLBACKS. Register CallbackReceiveMessageForPort and CallbackSendMessageForPort
/// before the first Tick().
/// Without CallbackReceiveMessageForPort the stack reads nothing, reports no error, and the
/// device is silently
/// deaf. Without CallbackSendMessageForPort it can answer nothing. Neither is optional in
/// practice.
///
/// On each call, uses the receive message callback to
/// get bytes from the socket, then processes them.Also handles any other clean - up or
/// maintenance functions
/// like COV expiration.
///
/// Returns true if any work was done during this tick, otherwise false.
/// Work is defined as :
/// -Processed an incoming BACnet message
/// - Sent a BACnet message
/// - Advanced BACnet/SC startup or connection state in a way that changed internal state or
