/// Adds a Lift or Escalator Object. The device must be added first before this function can be
/// called.
///
/// If adding to an Elevator Group Object, the Elevator Group object must be created first.
///
/// SIDE EFFECT: when elevatorGroupInstance is not 4194303, this object is also APPENDED to that
/// Elevator Group object's Group_Members property (135-2024 cl. 12.58.7). Note that
/// BACnetStack_SetLiftHigherLowerDeck can later REMOVE it again - see that function.
///
/// The only Lift/Escalator properties that are handled and stored by the CAS BACnet Stack are:
/// - ObjectIdentifier, ObjectType, PropertyList
/// - StatusFlags (assembled by the stack, but from EventState / Reliability / OutOfService,
/// which are themselves read back through the callbacks below)
/// - ElevatorGroup, GroupID and InstallationID (all set by this function)
/// - EnergyMeterRef, if BACnetStack_SetLiftOrEscalatorEnergyMeterRef was called. When it names
/// a real instance the stack then reports EnergyMeter as 0.0
/// - HigherDeck and LowerDeck, if BACnetStack_SetLiftHigherLowerDeck was called
///
/// THE DOOR COUNT IS NOT STORED BY THE STACK. Every door-indexed array below is served entirely
/// by
/// the application, which therefore owns how many doors the lift has.
///
/// Callbacks handle everything else. Required Lift properties:
///
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Property Datatype Callback
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// ObjectName CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
/// CarPosition Unsigned8 CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
/// CarMovingDirection Enumerated CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
/// CarDoorStatus Enumerated array CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
/// useArrayIndex = the door number
/// PassengerAlarm Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// OutOfService Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// CallbackSetPropertyBool (if made writable)
/// FaultSignals BACnetLIST of CallbackGetListOfEnumerations
/// Enumerated
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
///
/// Optional Lift properties - enable each with BACnetStack_SetPropertyEnabled first:
///
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Property Datatype Callback
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// FloorText, CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
/// CarDoorText array
/// MakingCarCall Unsigned8 array CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
/// CarDoorCommand Enumerated array CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
/// AssignedLandingCalls
/// BACnetAssigned CallbackGetSequenceLiftAssignedLandingCall
/// LandingCalls array
/// RegisteredCarCall BACnetLiftCarCall CallbackGetSequenceLiftRegisteredCarCall
/// List array
/// LandingDoorStatus BACnetLandingDoor CallbackGetSequenceLiftLandingDoorStatus
/// Status array
/// CarLoad Real CallbackGetPropertyReal
/// CarMode, Enumerated CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
/// CarDriveStatus,
/// CarAssignedDirection
/// CarDoorZone Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// NextStoppingFloor Unsigned8 CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
/// TimeDelay, Unsigned CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
/// TimeDelayNormal
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
///
/// Required Escalator properties. An Escalator has NO object-specific callbacks - everything is a
/// plain typed property:
///
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Property Datatype Callback
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// ObjectName CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
/// OperationDirection Enumerated CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
/// PassengerAlarm Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// OutOfService Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// PowerMode* Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// EscalatorMode* Enumerated CallbackGetPropertyEnumerated
/// FaultSignals* BACnetLIST of CallbackGetListOfEnumerations
/// Enumerated
/// Optional; enable it with BACnetStack_SetPropertyEnabled first. FaultSignals is
/// required on a Lift but optional on an Escalator.
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
///
/// IMPORTANT: CarPosition, CarMovingDirection, CarDoorStatus and PassengerAlarm on a Lift, and
/// OperationDirection and PassengerAlarm on an Escalator, return
/// Error(PROPERTY, VALUE_NOT_INITIALIZED) if the application does not serve them - the stack
/// deliberately refuses to invent a value for these. OutOfService is NOT in that set: an unserved
/// OutOfService silently reports FALSE.
///
/// NOTE: GroupID and InstallationID are stored by the stack but are Unsigned properties, and the
/// stack consults the callbacks BEFORE its own store. A registered
/// CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger that answers for either one OVERRIDES the value set here.
///
/// C declaration: `bool BACnetStack_AddLiftOrEscalatorObject(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const
/// uint16_t objectType, const uint32_t objectInstance, const uint32_t elevatorGroupInstance,
/// const uint8_t groupId, const uint8_t installationId)`
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `deviceInstance` - (in) The instance number of the device that owns this Lift or Escalator Object.
/// * `objectType` - (in) Must be Lift or Escalator. See #CASBACnetStack::BACnetObjectType. Any other value
///   is rejected.
/// * `objectInstance` - (in) The instance number of this Lift or Escalator Object.
/// * `elevatorGroupInstance` - (in) The instance number of the Elevator Group Object that this Lift or Escalator
///   Object belongs to. That object must already exist or this call fails. Use 4194303 -
///   the spec's "no reference" sentinel (cl. 12.59.6 / 12.60.6) - when this object is not
///   part of an Elevator Group Object.
/// * `groupId` - (in) Group_ID for this object, an Unsigned8 (cl. 12.59.7 / 12.60.7). Stored verbatim:
///   it is NOT validated, and it is NOT kept in sync with the referenced Elevator Group's
///   own Group_ID (cl. 12.58.6), so you must pass a value that matches the group yourself.
/// * `installationId` - (in) Installation_ID for this object, an Unsigned8 (cl. 12.59.8 / 12.60.8). The spec
///   requires this to be unique among the Lift or Escalator Objects of the same Elevator
///   Group Object, but the stack does NOT check it - a duplicate is stored and served
///   without complaint.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// True on success; false if the device does not exist, objectType is not Lift or Escalator,
/// the referenced Elevator Group Object does not exist, or Lift/Escalator support was not
/// compiled. On failure the partially created object is removed again.
pub fn BACnetStack_AddLiftOrEscalatorObject(
    deviceInstance: u32,
    objectType: u16,
    objectInstance: u32,
    elevatorGroupInstance: u32,
    groupId: u8,
    installationId: u8,
) -> BACnetResult<bool> {
    unsafe {
        let function: libloading::Symbol<unsafe extern "C" fn(u32, u16, u32, u32, u8, u8) -> bool> =
            LIBRARY.get(b"BACnetStack_AddLiftOrEscalatorObject")?;
        Ok(function(deviceInstance, objectType, objectInstance, elevatorGroupInstance, groupId, installationId))
    }
}

