/// Adds a File Object. The device must be added first before this function can be called.
/// The only File properties that are handled and stored by the CAS BACnet Stack are:
/// - FileAccessMethod (set by this function)
/// - PropertyList
///
/// Callbacks are used to handle other properties. The following list contains the required
/// properties
/// and the Callbacks that are used to get the required data:
///
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// Property Datatype Callback
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/// ObjectName CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
/// FileType CharacterString CallbackGetPropertyCharacterString
/// FileSize Unsigned CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
/// CallbackSetPropertyUnsignedInteger (if writable)
/// ModificationDate BACnetDateTime CallbackGetPropertyDate
/// CallbackGetPropertyTime
/// Archive Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// CallbackSetPropertyBool
/// ReadOnly Boolean CallbackGetPropertyBool
/// RecordCount* Unsigned CallbackGetPropertyUnsignedInteger
/// Only if FileAccessMethod is set to RecordAccess
/// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
///
/// Calling this function again for a File Object that already exists updates the property set to
/// match the
/// fileAccessMethod given on the later call:
/// - RecordCount is added or removed. ASHRAE 135-2024 Table 12-16 footnote 2 requires this: the
/// property "shall be present only if File_Access_Method is RECORD_ACCESS".
/// - FileSize is made writable for a writable stream-access file and non-writable otherwise. Only
/// the
/// first half is required (footnote 1: "If the file size can be changed by writing to the file,
/// and
/// File_Access_Method is STREAM_ACCESS, then this property shall be writable" - a sufficient
/// condition, not a prohibition). Withholding a writable FileSize from a record-access file is a
/// CAS BACnet Stack policy decision: cl. 12.13.6 defines writing FileSize in octets, which has no
/// defined meaning against record boundaries, and a record file resizes through RecordCount.
/// - The isConfigurationFile listing is add-only: a repeat call will not list the same object
/// twice,
/// but it also will not remove an object from ConfigurationFiles that an earlier call added.
///
/// DECLARED LIMIT for record access - at most 128 records per AtomicReadFile request, and at most
/// 2048
/// octets of record data. This is a deliberate bound (stack-allocated buffers, embedded targets)
/// and it
/// is a declared deviation from ASHRAE 135-2024 cl. 14.1.5, so it must be declared in the
/// PICS/EPICS of a
/// product built on this stack. See #BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReadFileRecord for the full
/// statement.
///
/// C declaration: `bool BACnetStack_AddFileObject(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const uint32_t
/// objectInstance, const bool isWritable, const bool isConfigurationFile, const uint8_t
/// fileAccessMethod)`
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `deviceInstance` - (in) The instance number of the device that owns this File Object.
/// * `objectInstance` - (in) The instance number of this File Object.
/// * `isWritable` - (in) A flag that determines if the file is writable. This sets the File's ReadOnly
///   property flag to true (if not writable) or false. If writable, the File's FileSize
///   property is made writable. The CAS BACnet Stack supports only writing a value of 0 to
///   the FileSize property which should delete all the contents of the file but not the
///   file itself.
/// * `isConfigurationFile` - (in) A flag that determines if the file is a configuration file. Configuration files
///   do not increment the DatabaseRevision property when they are added or removed.
/// * `fileAccessMethod` - (in) The File_Access_Method of this File Object: Record Access = 0, Stream Access = 1.
///   Any other value is rejected. Record-access File objects are served by the callbacks
///   registered with #BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackReadFileRecord /
///   #BACnetStack_RegisterCallbackWriteFileRecord, and their RecordCount property is
///   enabled automatically. See the repeat-call and record-limit notes above.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// True on success; false if the device does not exist, the object could not be added,
/// File-object support was not compiled, or one of the object's stored properties could not
/// be saved. IMPORTANT for that last case: the File object may ALREADY be present in
/// Object_List even though false was returned, missing File_Access_Method and/or
/// File_Read_Only - which makes every AtomicReadFile/AtomicWriteFile against it fail. Read
/// false as "this object is not usable" rather than "nothing happened", and remove the object
/// or restart configuration.
pub fn BACnetStack_AddFileObject(
    deviceInstance: u32,
    objectInstance: u32,
    isWritable: bool,
    isConfigurationFile: bool,
    fileAccessMethod: u8,
) -> BACnetResult<bool> {
    unsafe {
        let function: libloading::Symbol<unsafe extern "C" fn(u32, u32, bool, bool, u8) -> bool> =
            LIBRARY.get(b"BACnetStack_AddFileObject")?;
        Ok(function(deviceInstance, objectInstance, isWritable, isConfigurationFile, fileAccessMethod))
    }
}

// ---- Property Setup Functions ----

/// Enables a device or object property. The device and/or object must already exist.
/// This function is used primarly to enable optional properties. For example: description.
///
/// C declaration: `bool BACnetStack_SetPropertyEnabled(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const
/// uint16_t objectType, const uint32_t objectInstance, const uint32_t propertyIdentifier, const
/// bool enabled)`
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `deviceInstance` - (in) The instance number of the device that contains the object whose property will be
///   enabled.
/// * `objectType` - (in) The object type of the object whose property will be enabled. See
///   #CASBACnetStack::BACnetObjectType for more info.
/// * `objectInstance` - (in) The object instance of the object whose property will be enabled.
/// * `propertyIdentifier` - (in) The property to enable. See #BACnetPropertyIdentifier for more info.
/// * `enabled` - (in) True to enable, false to disable... Recommended value: true
///
/// # Returns
///
