/// Sets the COV subscription-table capacity and the maximum supported COV lifetime for
/// subscriptions received by this device.
///
/// The lifetime is a single device-wide bound shared by SubscribeCOV, SubscribeCOVProperty and
/// SubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple.
///
/// ENFORCEMENT IS REJECT, NOT CLAMP. A subscription request asking for a lifetime longer than
/// maxSupportedCOVLifetime is answered with Error(services, valueOutOfRange); it is not silently
/// shortened to the maximum.
///
/// THE DEVICE DEFAULT IS 28800 SECONDS (8 hours) - MAX_SUPPORTED_COV_LIFETIME in
/// BACnetStackConstants.h, the minimum the BACnet spec requires a device to support. Every device
/// starts at that value, so it is what the stack enforced before this setter was called.
///
/// PASS 0 FOR "USE THE DEVICE DEFAULT". A caller migrating from the removed
/// BACnetStack_SetMaxActiveCOVSubscriptions has no v5 lifetime to copy - that export never
/// expressed one - so 0 is accepted as the sentinel and substitutes 28800, making the migration
/// behaviour-preserving without the caller having to know the number. Passing 28800 explicitly is
/// identical. Issue #448.
///
/// NOTE 0 previously meant the near OPPOSITE of "default": a zero bound rejected every request
/// carrying a non-zero lifetime (they all exceed the maximum) while still admitting indefinite,
/// lifetime-0 subscriptions. If you deliberately want that behaviour, it is no longer reachable
/// through this export. maxNumberOfSubscriptions = 0 continues to mean NO LIMIT.
///
/// #931: THIS FUNCTION IS NOT ATOMIC. It applies maxNumberOfSubscriptions first, then
/// maxSupportedCOVLifetime; if the second application fails, the first has ALREADY taken effect
/// and
/// this still returns false - the caller cannot tell a total failure from a half-applied one. The
/// two
/// settings are independent, so prefer the single-purpose
/// BACnetStack_SetMaxActiveCOVSubscriptions and
/// BACnetStack_SetMaxSupportedCOVLifetime below, each of which is unambiguous about what it
/// changed.
/// This function is kept for compatibility with its existing partial-application behaviour.
///
/// C declaration: `bool BACnetStack_SetCOVSettings(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const uint32_t
/// maxNumberOfSubscriptions, const uint32_t maxSupportedCOVLifetime)`
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `deviceInstance` - (in) The instance of the device to set the maximum supported COV lifetime.
/// * `maxNumberOfSubscriptions` - (in) The maximum number of active COV subscriptions to support. If set to zero, no
///   limit.
/// * `maxSupportedCOVLifetime` - (in) The maximum supported COV lifetime in seconds. Valid range is 0 .. MAX_UINT32 -
///   1; exactly MAX_UINT32 is rejected. Pass 28800 for the device default. See the note
///   above before passing 0.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// True if successful, false if failed.
pub fn BACnetStack_SetCOVSettings(
    deviceInstance: u32,
    maxNumberOfSubscriptions: u32,
    maxSupportedCOVLifetime: u32,
) -> BACnetResult<bool> {
    unsafe {
        let function: libloading::Symbol<unsafe extern "C" fn(u32, u32, u32) -> bool> =
            LIBRARY.get(b"BACnetStack_SetCOVSettings")?;
        Ok(function(deviceInstance, maxNumberOfSubscriptions, maxSupportedCOVLifetime))
    }
}

