/// Configures a Channel object's stack-held data: the concrete primitive datatype of its
/// Present_Value
/// (a BACnetChannelValue CHOICE) and an initially-empty List_Of_Object_Property_References.
///
/// TRAP: the datatype is FIXED here, at configuration time. 135-2024 cl. 12.53.5 defines
/// Present_Value as whatever was most recently written to it, so a Channel whose clients write
/// more
/// than one datatype cannot be modelled through this export - the stored code is what the stack
/// uses
/// to dispatch every Present_Value read to a typed Get callback.
