// ---- Data Notification Functions ----

/// Tells the CAS BACnet Stack that a value has changed, and runs every piece of logic attached to
/// that
/// data point: COV and COV-property-multiple notifications, COV-driven trend logging, the
/// deferred
/// BUFFER_READY evaluation for any trend log that grew, and the intrinsic event and fault
/// algorithms.
///
/// REQUIRED. Every algorithm armed by the BACnetStack_SetIntrinsic* and BACnetStack_SetFault*
/// functions is DORMANT until this function is called for the monitored property - typically
/// Present_Value, but Total_Record_Count for BUFFER_READY, Member_Status_Flags for a globalGroup
/// and
/// Timer_State for a timer. A host that never calls it will never generate an event notification.
///
/// C declaration: `bool BACnetStack_UpdateValue(const uint32_t deviceInstance, const uint16_t
/// objectType, const uint32_t objectInstance, const uint32_t propertyIdentifier)`
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * `deviceInstance` - (in) The instance of the device that contains the object where the value changed.
/// * `objectType` - (in) The BACnet object type of the object where the value changed. See
///   #CASBACnetStack::BACnetObjectType for more info.
/// * `objectInstance` - (in) The instance of the object where the value changed.
/// * `propertyIdentifier` - (in) The property of the value that changed. See #BACnetPropertyIdentifier for more
///   info.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// True if the value update was processed. False if the device does not exist, if the
/// property is not enabled on that object, or - TRAP - if the device advertises SubscribeCOV
/// or SubscribeCOVProperty but the build did not define STACK_OPTION_SUBSCRIBE_COV, in which
/// case this returns BEFORE the alarm and event evaluation runs at all. A second trap: for
/// propertyIdentifier Object_Name or Object_Identifier the device's Database_Revision is
/// incremented BEFORE the property-enabled check, so a call that returns false can still have
/// bumped the revision.
