/// Registers the callback the stack calls to apply an AtomicWriteFile request. Called from inside
/// BACnetStack_Tick().
///
/// fileStart IS SIGNED AND -1 MEANS APPEND. The stack passes -1 straight through (135-2024
/// cl. 14.2.1.3.1 / 14.2.2.3.1) and only rejects values below -1 before calling you. You MUST
/// resolve
/// -1 to the real position the write began at and report it in ackFileStart, because that value
/// is
/// copied verbatim into the AtomicWriteFile-ACK. ackFileStart is OUT-only, preset to 0; a
/// negative
/// value left there after a successful write is logged but still sent, and fails 135.1-2023
/// 9.13.1.1.3.
///
/// ONLY TWO ERROR CODES SURVIVE. errorCode is preset to success; on a false return the stack
/// honours
/// invalidFileStartPosition (class SERVICES) and fileFull (class OBJECT), and collapses
/// everything
