/// Sends an unconfirmed COV notification unprompted by any subscription (cl. 13.1.1), used by a
/// device to announce a value on its own initiative rather than in response to SubscribeCOV.
///
/// #1013: clause 21.3.2's UnconfirmedCOVNotification-Request has FIVE required fields. Until now
/// this
/// export could only supply two of them meaningfully - subscriber-process-identifier and
/// time-remaining were hardwired to 0, and list-of-values carried exactly one property with no
/// array
/// index, so the Present_Value + Status_Flags pair clause 13.1 expects a notification to carry
/// could
/// not be sent at all. All three are now parameters.
///
/// VALUES COME FROM THIS DEVICE'S OWN DATABASE, not from the caller (#1013 action item 4, decided
/// 2026-09-08 - see the issue). `initiatingDeviceInstance` must name a device added with
/// BACnetStack_AddDevice, and each property's value is read from it exactly as a ReadProperty
/// would.
/// A gateway announcing on behalf of a device it proxies models that device as a VIRTUAL device
/// (BACnetStack_AddVirtualNetwork + BACnetStack_AddDeviceToVirtualNetwork) and announces from it
/// -
/// at which point the values are local and this rule holds. Supplying values through the call
/// instead would need a datatype-plus-bytes encoding per property, a far larger surface, and
/// would
/// let a caller announce a value the device would not itself report.
///
/// `properties` is `propertyCount` packed elements, little-endian, each a FIXED 9 BYTES - the
/// same
/// shape convention as BACnetStack_SendSubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple's `references`:
///
/// -[0]---------*-[1..4]--------------*-[5..8]---------------*
/// | uint8 flags | uint32 propertyId | uint32 arrayIndex |
/// -------------*---------------------*----------------------*
///
/// flags: bit0 = usePropertyArrayIndex (when clear, arrayIndex is ignored and the whole property
/// is
/// sent). Every element names a property of the SAME monitored object - the object identifier is
/// already given by monitoredObjectType/monitoredObjectInstance.
///
/// `propertiesLength` is the total byte length of `properties` and must be at least
/// propertyCount * 9; a shorter buffer is DETECTED and rejected rather than over-read.
/// `propertyCount` must be at least 1.
///
/// Worked example - announce Present_Value, no array index:
/// 00 55 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 (9 bytes total)
/// |fl| |propertyId ||arrayIndex |
/// propertyCount = 1, propertiesLength = 9. (propertyIdentifier 85 = Present_Value.)
