/// BACnetStack_SendWriteGroup (Sprint 261 item 13-send - moved to public + packed buffer, cl.
/// 15.11,
/// unconfirmed-service-choice 10). Distributes values to the Channel objects of a numbered
/// control group.
/// `changeList` is `changeListCount` packed elements, each 6 BYTES of header + a variable-length
/// value.
/// Multi-byte SCALAR HEADER fields are little-endian; the buffer is fully packed, no padding.
///
/// *-[0][1]------------*-[2]---------------------*-[3]----------------*-[4][5]-------------*-[6+]-
/// Variable -*
/// | uint16_t channel | uint8_t overridPriority | uint8_t dataType | uint16_t valueLen | value
/// bytes |
/// *-------------------*-------------------------*--------------------*--------------------*-----------------*
///
/// overridingPriority 0 = absent (valid priorities 1..16). dataType is a BACnet primitive
/// application tag.
/// `changeListLength` is the total byte length of `changeList` - the sum over all elements of (6
/// + valueLen).
/// Elements are NOT a fixed stride.
///
/// VALUE ENCODING - READ THIS. #1594 ruled 2026-09-09: the `value bytes` are the value's RAW
/// BINARY
/// wire form, NOT ASCII/UTF-8 text (this replaces the pre-2026-09-09 text convention - a hard
/// cutover,
/// not a dual-supported option; see docs/sprints/wp3-value-encoding-proposal.md for the full
/// table).
/// The stack parses them with BACnetAbstractSyntaxType::DecodeBinary(dataType, ...). Multi-byte
/// numeric fields are little-endian, matching every other scalar field in this buffer:
/// Null -> 0 bytes (valueLen 0)
/// Boolean -> 1 byte: 0x00 or 0x01
/// UnsignedInteger -> 4 bytes, uint32_t, little-endian
/// SignedInteger -> 4 bytes, int32_t, little-endian, two's complement
/// Real -> 4 bytes, IEEE-754 float, little-endian (e.g. 23.5f -> 00 00 BC 41)
/// Double -> 8 bytes, IEEE-754 double, little-endian
/// OctetString -> raw bytes, as-is (valueLen-bounded)
/// CharacterString -> raw UTF-8 bytes, as-is (valueLen-bounded)
/// BitString -> 1 byte "unused bits in last octet" (0..7, ASHRAE cl. 20.2.10) + packed
/// octets, MSB-first within each octet
/// Enumerated -> 4 bytes, uint32_t, little-endian
/// Date -> 4 bytes: yearMinus1900, month, day, weekday (0xFF = wildcard per field)
/// Time -> 4 bytes: hour, minute, second, hundredths (0xFF = wildcard per field)
/// BACnetObjectIdentifier -> 6 bytes: uint16_t objectType (LE) + uint32_t objectInstance (LE) -
/// the two-field split, NOT the internal packed-32-bit form
/// DateTime -> 8 bytes: Date (4) then Time (4), concatenated
/// DeviceObjectPropertyReference is not supported on this export. DecodeBinary checks length
/// before
/// content, so passing the old TEXT form USUALLY fails the decode and returns false - but this is
/// NOT guaranteed for every value: a text value whose character count happens to equal its type's
/// binary width passes the length check and is silently misinterpreted (e.g. Real "23.5" is 4
/// ASCII
/// bytes, the same width as a 4-byte float, so it decodes as garbage instead of failing).
/// Re-encode
/// every caller of this export in the new binary form - do not rely on the decode failing to
/// catch
/// a caller you missed.
///
/// Worked example - channel 7, no overriding priority, Real 23.5:
/// 07 00 00 04 04 00 00 00 BC 41 (10 bytes total)
/// |chan| |pri||typ| |len| | 23.5f as IEEE-754 LE |
/// changeListCount = 1, changeListLength = 10.
///
/// NOTE: this now matches the convention already used by the `references` buffer of
/// BACnetStack_SendSubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple below, whose covIncrement is a RAW 4-byte
/// little-endian IEEE-754 float - covIncrement was the precedent this format follows.
///
/// Use your language adapter's WriteGroup packer to build the buffer rather than packing it by
/// hand.
/// All seven adapters ship one and all seven agree with the encoding described above:
/// adapters/csharp/PropertyBufferHelper.cs adapters/java/.../PropertyBufferHelper.java
/// adapters/python/property_buffer_helper.py adapters/rust/property_buffer_helper.rs
/// adapters/golang/propertybufferhelper/ adapters/cpp/CASBACnetStackPackHelpers.h
/// adapters/node/.../property-arrays.ts
/// Returns true on success.
///
/// C declaration: `bool BACnetStack_SendWriteGroup(const uint32_t groupNumber, const uint8_t
/// writePriority, const uint32_t changeListCount, const void* changeList, const uint32_t
